drm/msm/a6xx: Distinguish an unobserved RSCC stop from an ACK

If there is no firmware start recorded, no RSCC sleep request or poll
runs. Return -ENODATA in that branch, not successful acknowledgement.
Report the distinction internally without changing PM callbacks, power
operations, or teardown. No ACK, including a reported success, alone
establishes terminal DMA isolation.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -661,8 +661,9 @@
 	int ret;
 	u32 val;
 
+	/* No firmware start recorded: no RSCC acknowledgement was sampled. */
 	if (!test_and_clear_bit(GMU_STATUS_FW_START, &gmu->status))
-		return 0;
+		return -ENODATA;
 
 	if (adreno_is_a840(adreno_gpu) || adreno_is_a850_family(adreno_gpu))
 		bitmask = BIT(30);
@@ -1532,7 +1533,9 @@
 	else
 		stop_ret = a6xx_gmu_shutdown(gmu);
 
-	if (stop_ret)
+	if (stop_ret == -ENODATA)
+		dev_dbg(gmu->dev, "GMU stop: no RSCC sleep acknowledgement sampled\n");
+	else if (stop_ret)
 		dev_err_ratelimited(gmu->dev,
 				    "GMU stop not fully acknowledged: %d\n", stop_ret);
